    "b-sks-rc-ks-intro": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM — Three contracts carry what the harness thinks it knows. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "fact",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the atom: one row per live claim about one subject (a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "target",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " or an "
        },
        {
          "insert": "entity",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "), carrying a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "rationale",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and its own "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows, overwritten in place. The knowledge record is not a table: it is the derived view that assembles one subject's live facts, linked subjects, and cited observations into a page. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows are fact-owned citations: each points into one knowledge source through a typed "
        },
        {
          "insert": "locator",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and says why that observation supports the claim; they are written with their fact and die with it. A "
        },
        {
          "insert": "link",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " carries its own inline pointer and never references the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " table; the fact's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "rationale",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the argument from those observations to the claim. The librarian is the only writer on this side of the model; there is no "
        },
        {
          "insert": "updated_by",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " anywhere in the knowledge system."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-sks-rc-ks-intro",
      "children": []
    },
